      "message": "perf(geometry): linear spline speed bound and a bounded near-round ellipse\n\nReview of PR #3958, the two optional items:\n- The non-rational test of the spline speed bound is computed once per\n  curve, not for each span (40,000 collinear controls in a debug build:\n  13.8 s before, 0.5 s after).\n- A near-round ELLIPSE is a circle only when radius * (1 - ratio) is\n  within the curve tolerance; the document then records the tolerance.\n  Otherwise the ellipse is fitted with arcs.\n\nRefs #1865\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
